 LIBERAL CENSORSHIP

  A familiar chant emanating from conservatives
 counterdemonstrating against the left is: _Take a bath, get a
 job._  The leftists who founded People for the American Way (PAW)
 heeded this advice.
  You can dress them up, the old saying goes, but you still can_t
 take them out.  The politics of these left-wingers in suits and
 ties still shines through.
  In August, PAW released Attacks on the Freedom to Learn, their
 9th annual report on _school censorship and related attacks on the
 public schools._  PAW President Arthur J. Kropp declared the
 1990-91 school year was _the single worst year...in the history of
 our research._
  PAW research, found _national conservative groups have retaken
 the censorship initiative._  He noted, _It is diversity that the
 censors find most disturbing....Just as the art, film, and
 television programs that the extremists challenge are targeted for
 their depiction of diverse lifestyles, beliefs, and experiences,
 so too are public school materials challenged for nothing more
 sinister than depicting diversity, telling the truth about
 troubling issues, or telling children to face up to problems and
 take responsibility._
  The _extremists_disagreed.  _Who are the real censors?_ asks
 Concerned Women for America (CWA) President Beverly LaHaye.  _The
 fact is, PAW criticizes parents who exercise their rightful role
 in determining how their children should be educated._
  Dealing with CWA, PAW acted as the censor and shot itself in the
 foot.  CWA Press Secretary Caia Mockaitis showed up at the
 presentation of the report, but was denied access to the room.
 PAW_s act of censoring its opposition was its downfall when press
 reports of the event mentioned the action.
  Phyllis Schlafly, president of Eagle Forum, pointed out in her
 syndicated column that the alleged censorship of Little Red Riding
 Hood (called a _classic_) was actually the judgment call of a
 principal who felt a version of the fairy tale having Little Red
 bringing a bottle of wine to her red-nosed grandmother a bit out
 of step with the school_s anti-drug program.  Schlafly called the
 report a _gimmick_ to create _tear-jerking fund-raising letters_
 to PAWs over 300,000 donors.
  Upon closer scrutiny, it seems PAW and its liberal allies stand
 by in muted silence as education is hijacked and perverted by the
 left and its causes.
  In his statement, Kropp said that _schools should help give
 students the tools they need to navigate the troubled waters of
 modern life._  Calming some of these _troubled waters_ included
 teaching children _to stay off drugs and alcohol._  They seem to
 have no problem, however, when federal money for anti-drug
 programs is diverted to fund the _Bridge-the-Gap Intergenerational
 Play Day_ in New York, where young homosexuals are given the
 opportunity to meet with their older counterparts.
  One of the featured guests of the Department of Education-funded
 Youth Enrichment Services (YES) program, which sponsored the _Play
 Day,_ was _Empress_ Razor Sharp of the Imperial Court of New York,
 a transvestite collective.  Since 1988, YES had received $510,000
 in grants, according to The New York Guardian.
  Senator Jesse Helms (R-NC) also lodged a complaint that San
 Francisco Superintendent of Schools Ramon C. Cortines used $31,643
 from the Drug-Free Schools and Communities Program and Centers for
 Disease Control to provide _a safe and nurturing environment_ for
 homosexuals and _make information available to students and staff
 to demystify homosexuality and recognize the contribution of gay
 and lesbian persons to our culture and history._
  The liberals have yet to voice their outrage over misusing funds
 on special interest programs.  Then again, one must remember that
 liberals like special interests.
  Another censorship outrage Kropp mentioned was the attempted
 banning of Webster_s Ninth Collegiate Dictionary where _the
 occasional four-letter word might appear._  Imagine the horror of
 a broad-based campaign to ban the dictionary.  It was, however,
 only in liberal dreams.  In reality, the person asking that the
 dictionary be removed from the library because of profanity never
 completed the proper forms and garnered only five signatures on a
 petition.  The school board voted in support of the dictionary,
 but only in an informal nature.
  Even though the alleged conservative censorship was negligible in
 that case, what about liberal influence on the current dictionary?
 The newest edition of the dictionary that was _under threat_ from
 conservatives contains new terms that can definitely enjoy the
 _politically correct_ stamp of approval.  The recently-released
 edition contains new terms such as _womyn,_ _weightism,_ and
 _outing._  Concerning obscenities, Reinhold Aman reveals in
 Maledicta X a pecking order for slurs.  In Webster_s New World
 Dictionary (Third College Edition), he points out that many
 _common slurs_ are omitted as well as the development a ranking:
 _nigger_ is considered _viciously hostile,_ _kike_ is _vulgar,_
 but "frog" (Frenchman) or "Kraut" contain no such adjectival
 warning.
  The examples go on and on.  Sure there is censorship on both
 sides, PAW admits it, but they fail to put their money where their
 mouth is.  As is tradition for the left, they are content to let
 their own garden run afoul while castigating the neighbors about
 theirs.  This has got to stop.  They must be held accountable as
 well.
